<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4.3 Additional ablations ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Hybrid Reinforcement:When Reward Is Sparse, It’s Better to Be Dense" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Dense negative ranges are more important than positive samples.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" title="In 4.3 Additional ablations ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Hybrid Reinforcement:When Reward Is Sparse, It’s Better to Be Dense" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Reward range selection is crucial for balancing stability and performance.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3" title="In 4.3 Additional ablations ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Hybrid Reinforcement:When Reward Is Sparse, It’s Better to Be Dense" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Variance-aware reweighting in <span class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HERO</span> improves model’s reasoning ability.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4" title="In 4.3 Additional ablations ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Hybrid Reinforcement:When Reward Is Sparse, It’s Better to Be Dense" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">The proposed method does not rely on large reward models.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
